gtasks-panel (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Own GTK 3 window instead of the Chrome app window. One click on the
    panel item opens a popup with the open tasks, two clicks open the
    full window with lists, tasks and a detail pane.
  * New command gtasks-window and desktop entry com.belneiski.gtasks.
  * Add, complete, un-complete, edit title, notes and due date, move to
    another list, delete with an undo bar, show completed.
  * Read-write scope https://www.googleapis.com/auth/tasks. A 0.1.0
    token is read-only, so run "gtasks-panel --auth" one time again.
  * Code moved into the private package /usr/share/gtasks-panel.
  * Task cache in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/gtasks-panel/tasks.json: the window
    opens at once and works offline.
  * Drop gtasks-open, wmctrl and the Chrome and terminal recommends.
  * After an upgrade run "gtasks-window --quit" one time: the old
    process stays resident.

 -- Pencho BELNEYSKI <pencho@belneiski.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:49:38 +0200

